      "id": "WORMS-206982",
      "title": "Stylophora pistillata (Esper, 1792) taxon record (accepted; family Pocilloporidae; common names hood coral, pistillate coral). Description: branches stoutest in shallow water; calices 0.5 to 1.5 mm diameter, scattered irregularly and closely, usually hooded by a projection of coenosteum on the side of the calice towards the branch tip; six primary septa and a small columella; ends of branches blunt and often slightly club-shaped; colour cream, pink, blue or green; polyps extended only at night.",
      "publisher": "World Register of Marine Species (World List of Scleractinia, Hoeksema, Cairns and Samimi-Namin)",
